Not all logos stick. Some are forgotten the moment you look away. Others stay with you for years. The difference isn't always about budget — it's about the principles behind the design.

## Simplicity

Memorable logos are almost always simple. This seems counterintuitive — surely more detail means more effort, more quality? In practice, the opposite is true. Simple logos are easier to recognise at a glance, easier to reproduce at any size, and easier to remember.

A complex logo with fine detail may look impressive on a large screen, but it loses its impact as a favicon, on a business card, or on a van viewed from a distance. Simplicity ensures the logo works everywhere.

## Distinctiveness

A memorable logo looks different from what else is in the market. If every business in your industry uses similar fonts, colours, and shapes, blending in is easy. Standing out takes intentional design choices.

Distinctiveness doesn't mean being outlandish — it means having a visual identity that is clearly, recognisably yours.

## Relevance

The best logos communicate something about the business — not always literally, but through visual cues that feel right. Colours, shapes, and typography all carry associations. A law firm logo looks different from a children's entertainment logo for good reasons.

This doesn't mean your logo needs to be a literal illustration of what you do. An abstract mark that uses the right visual language for your industry can be more effective than a clipart image of your product.

## Versatility

A strong logo works in one colour, in reverse (white on a dark background), at any size, and across every application you need. If a logo only works in full colour at a specific size, it's going to cause problems in the real world.

## Timelessness

Trend-led logos — designs that lean heavily on whatever is fashionable at the moment — date quickly. A logo designed now with overtly trendy fonts and effects may look visibly dated within a few years. Good logo design aims for something that will remain relevant for many years.

